        "lib/features/reminders/data/platform_reminder_scheduler.dart",
        "docs/field/2026-08-09-current-release-readiness.md"
      ],
      "disposition": "iOS project target13 versus framework metadata12 is not by itself an app deployment contradiction. CocoaPods files/includes and notification delegate assignment required by the explicitly release-excluded iOS oracle are absent. Reminder target selection includes iOS; this is an unverified integration boundary, not a passing delivery claim. macOS scaffold target10.14/sandbox lacks network-client/media/user-selected-file grants and media privacy strings. Android release evidence does not certify Apple; no active Apple artifact acceptance was found. Retain these prerequisites in G8.3 platform support disposition and B19 platform matrix: either explicit unsupported capability gates or native integration/regression before any support claim. Empty Apple tests prove no native behavior. No Apple production runtime defect is fabricated from scaffold alone."
    },
    {
      "id": "REV10-X04",
      "key": "windows",
      "title": "Windows runner failure paths",
      "evidence": [
        "windows/runner/utils.cpp",
        "windows/runner/main.cpp",
        "windows/runner/flutter_window.cpp",
        "windows/runner/win32_window.cpp"
      ],
      "disposition": "REV10-03 retains conversion allocation candidate and REV10-04 retains font-message lifetime candidate. GetMessage(-1) is treated as truthy, but the current unfiltered null-HWND call has no demonstrated invalid-handle/filter path; do not assert a live loop failure. Early Create failure returns without CoUninitialize but exits this process, so no persistent COM leak is demonstrated. freopen_s condition is inverted, yet reopening stdout/stderr itself handles normal redirection; no demonstrated user failure from redundant dup2 is promoted. CMake/resources/version fallback are scaffold, not signing or binary provenance proof."
    },
    {
